{
  "Election": {
    "election_id": "k7pfqt",
    "title": "BV2266 — Two-seat board by Bloc STAR: the candidate who beats every rival is seated second",
    "description": "Seven voters, four candidates, two seats. Anika beats every rival head to head - Anika over Bo 4-2, over Cora 5-2, and over Dev 4-3 - so she is the Condorcet winner of this electorate. She is seated SECOND. Seat 1 - scores Dev 24, Bo 22, Anika 21, Cora 15, so Anika misses the automatic runoff by a single point and Dev wins it 2-1. Seat 2 - Dev is removed, and Anika beats Bo 4-2. The point is what seat order does and does not mean: under Bloc STAR the order is the order the runoffs finish in, not a ranking of how much the voters want each winner. That matters wherever the top finisher gets something extra - the chair, the longer term, the tie-breaking vote. The honest other half: counted for ONE seat these same ballots elect Dev and Anika loses outright, so the second seat is what rescues the majority-preferred candidate. No tie-break is used. Full lesson & tabulation: https://masiarek.github.io/star-voting-library/02_STAR_Bloc/03_Criteria/seat_order/index.html",
